    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d613-a1">

                <pb facs="1128" n="1004" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg1004"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 74.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Foster to Mr.
                            White.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >St. Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1880-12-14"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 14,
                        1880</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Colleague</hi>: On the 18th of October last I
                    acknowledged receipt of your letter regarding Mr. Wilczynski’s expulsion from
                    St. Petersburg, and wrote you a second letter on the subject in October.</p>
                <p>I now have the answer of the minister of foreign affairs to my application for
                    Mr. Wilczynski’s free return to St. Petersburg. He states that Mr. W. will be
                    permitted to return to this city and remain for six months, and that the
                    authorities have been <pb facs="1129" n="1005" xml:id="pg1005"/> so notified.
                    This is the extreme limit of time allowed by the laws of Russia to all
                    foreigners, without distinction, entering with a passport of their nationality,
                    at the expiration of which time they are required to obtain a Russian passport,
                    or police permission of residence, if they wish to remain.</p>
                <p>I return the passport which you sent me.</p>
                <p>Very truly, &amp;c.</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN W. FOSTER.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
